From 80d3f7bd0dfb9a2152fdc0b3b02411e1f7ebd676 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claud McClaudeson <claud@pantsforbirds.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:08:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] sw DOCX: tables beside a wrapped image like Word 2007 and
 Word 2013

A table that overlaps an image with parallel wrap is shifted below the
image in Word 2013+ (DOCX compatibilityMode 15). Word <= 2010 narrows an
autofit table without a preferred width instead, so that the text area
of its cells ends where the image's wrap area starts. Only the last
column gets narrower. The rest of a table continued on a next page, and
other tables, are shifted below the image.

Two problems in SwTabFrame::CalcFlyOffsets():

- The overlap check used the current print area of the table, which an
  earlier call may have narrowed already for a right-aligned image. Then
  there was no overlap and the narrowing stayed. Check against the print
  area without fly offsets instead: factor the left/right spacing out of
  SwTabFrame::Format() into CalcHoriSpacing().
- In compat mode <= 14 (ADD_FLY_OFFSETS), narrow autofit tables. Writer
  has no autofit tables, so the DOCX import notes this in the table grab
  bag ("TableAutoFit": tblLayout is not fixed and tblW has no width).
  SwCellFrame::Format() keeps the width of all but the last cell of such
  a narrowed table.

Change-Id: I54fc81b0f32e94fc3ab9f3dac2fdcf11c3a34a38
